<title>HUNGARY: Central Europe's CESI index ends slightly weaker.</title>
<headline>Central Europe's CESI index ends slightly weaker.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index eased on Thursday to end at 1,533.08 points, down 3.26 points or 0.21 percent, the Budapest Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index weakened as most shares in the basket closed lower.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
